0
-- the variable names the level in force, and every spelling sets it
default: warning
-d 2: info
-d debug: debug
set -d 0: error
a number is stored as its name: trace
hibr: HIBR_LOGLEVEL: loud is not a level: error, warning, info, debug, trace, or 0 to 4
refused, status 1, still warning
hibr: HIBR_LOGLEVEL: 9 is not a level: error, warning, info, debug, trace, or 0 to 4
-d 9: status 2
in f: error
after f: info
hibr: getopts: illegal option -z
unset: back to warning, []
-- a child: forked keeps it, a new shell takes it only when exported
hibr: log level info
subshell: info
new shell: warning
exported: info
environment, then -d: info
hibr: HIBR_LOGLEVEL: loud is not a level: error, warning, info, debug, trace, or 0 to 4
an environment naming no level: status 0, warning
HIBR_DEBUG is gone: warning
-- in the log, each level below error says its name
T hibr: nosuch_ll: command not found
T hibr: warning: getopts: illegal option -z
T hibr: trace: subscript -1 counts back to 1
T hibr: debug: EPOCHSECONDS is a clock; the assignment is ignored
T hibr: info: disowned job [1]
-- outside the log nothing is tagged
hibr: getopts: illegal option -z
hibr: getopts: illegal option -z
-- a warning collapsed keeps its name
T hibr: warning: getopts: illegal option -z
T   at rep.hibr:2
T hibr: warning: getopts: illegal option -z
T   at rep.hibr:2, came 2 times more in N s
-- agent mode's JSON is keyed by the level
{"warning":"getopts: illegal option -z","file":"command line","line":1}
{"error":"nosuch_ll: command not found","file":"command line","line":1}
